Title:

Automated Podcast Transcription and Topic Segmentation Using NLP
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 Overview:

This project focuses on building an automated system that converts podcast or audio recordings into structured textual information. The system performs audio cleaning, speech-to-text transcription, text preprocessing, topic segmentation, keyword extraction, and visualization.
Manual transcription and analysis of long audio files is time-consuming and inefficient. This project automates the entire pipeline, enabling users to quickly understand audio content through text and visual analytics.
A user-friendly interface allows users to upload and select transcripts, listen to cleaned audio, view segmented text, search keywords, and analyze data using charts and word clouds.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 Approach:

Audio Input
Raw audio files are taken from the dataset.
Audio Cleaning
Noise removal and audio enhancement is performed to improve clarity.
Speech Transcription
Cleaned audio is converted into text.
Text Preprocessing
Removing unnecessary symbols, headers, and stop words.
Converting text into a clean format.
Topic Segmentation
Long transcripts are divided into meaningful segments.
Keyword Extraction
Important words are extracted based on frequency.
Visualization
Bar charts for word frequency.
Word cloud for keyword distribution.
User Interface
Streamlit-based interface for easy interaction.
